{"task":"transcribe","language":"english","duration":44.58000183105469,"text":"In 1508, Pope Julius II asked Michelangelo, who thought of himself as a sculptor and not a painter, to paint the ceiling of this chapel. It is about 35 meters long and 14 wide, 500 square meters. For four years he worked standing on scaffolding with his head tipped back, and he never lay down, whatever the stories say. He even wrote a poem about how much his neck and back hurt. Down the middle he painted nine scenes from the beginning of the world, with more than 300 figures in all. The most famous is the creation of Adam, two fingers almost touching. Twenty-five years later he came back and painted the whole wall behind the altar.","words":[{"word":"In","start":0,"end":0.4399999976158142},{"word":"1508","start":0.4399999976158142,"end":1.600000023841858},{"word":"Pope","start":1.899999976158142,"end":2.0199999809265137},{"word":"Julius","start":2.0199999809265137,"end":2.4200000762939453},{"word":"II","start":2.4200000762939453,"end":2.9800000190734863},{"word":"asked","start":2.9800000190734863,"end":3.4800000190734863},{"word":"Michelangelo","start":3.4800000190734863,"end":4.199999809265137},{"word":"who","start":4.380000114440918,"end":4.860000133514404},{"word":"thought","start":4.860000133514404,"end":5},{"word":"of","start":5,"end":5.440000057220459},{"word":"himself","start":5.440000057220459,"end":5.440000057220459},{"word":"as","start":5.440000057220459,"end":5.71999979019165},{"word":"a","start":5.71999979019165,"end":6.059999942779541},{"word":"sculptor","start":6.059999942779541,"end":6.260000228881836},{"word":"and","start":6.260000228881836,"end":6.539999961853027},{"word":"not","start":6.539999961853027,"end":6.659999847412109},{"word":"a","start":6.659999847412109,"end":7.139999866485596},{"word":"painter","start":7.139999866485596,"end":7.139999866485596},{"word":"to","start":7.639999866485596,"end":7.840000152587891},{"word":"paint","start":7.840000152587891,"end":8},{